   "evidence": "Proof body: `h\u2082 : (2 : R) \u2022 (D : Module.End R (Octonion R)) x = 0` then `eq_zero_or_eq_zero_of_smul_eq_zero h\u2082 |>.resolve_left (NeZero.ne (2 : R))` \u2014 only 2-regularity of the module is consumed; grep shows no `NoZeroSMulDivisors` instance for `Octonion` in code/TauCeti.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Algebra/Octonion/Derivation.lean",
   "fix": "Factor the content into a theorem taking the 2-regularity hypothesis, e.g. `theorem derivation_eq_zero_of_imaginary (h2 : \u2200 y : Octonion R, (2 : R) \u2022 y = 0 \u2192 y = 0) ...` (or `IsSMulRegular (Octonion R) (2 : R)`), and register the instance from `[Invertible (2 : R)]` \u2014 the CommRing-level convention already used in the repo at TauCeti/RingTheory/Idempotents/SquareRootOne.lean:60 and TauCeti/RingTheory/Polynomial/Chebyshev/Basis.lean:30 \u2014 keeping the current pair only if a `\u2124`-style base is wanted as a second instance.",
   "issue": "`instIsFaithfulImaginaryLieSubmodule [NoZeroSMulDivisors R (Octonion R)] [NeZero (2 : R)]` is stronger than the argument: the proof only uses `(2 : R) \u2022 y = 0 \u2192 y = 0` (lines 311-315), yet `NoZeroSMulDivisors R (Octonion R)` rules out every base with zero divisors. It fails for `R = ZMod 9` (`3 \u2022 \u27e83,0,0,0\u27e9 = 0`) and `R = \u211a \u00d7 \u211a` (`(1,0) \u2022 \u27e8(0,1),0,0,0\u27e9 = 0`), where `2` is a unit and faithfulness plainly holds; nothing in `Octonion/Basic.lean` supplies a `NoZeroSMulDivisors` instance for `Octonion R` either, so outside `GroupWithZero.toNoZeroSMulDivisors` (mathlib/Mathlib/Algebra/NoZeroSMulDivisors/Basic.lean:30, i.e. fields) the instance does not even fire.",
   "line": 299
  }
 ],
